{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fibre-products}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b73ee394f2f90c545116c197e886bf78e639e65351e5ea36c5662beb7e4a99ed", "source_text": "Fibre products", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3fb328240f14a6c683dadd915dba35c9732726c0fcd8393dd31471b48c12dc5", "unit_id": "tag:072L:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& ? \\ar@{..>}[rd] \\ar@{..>}[ld] \\\\\nS \\ar[rd]_{(E, f, 0)} & & S' \\ar[ld]^{(E', f', 0')} \\\\\n& \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$?$", "MATH_0004": "$(a, a', \\alpha)$", "MATH_0005": "$a : T \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$a' : T \\to S'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\alpha : E \\times_{S, a} T \\to E' \\times_{S', a'} T$", "MATH_0008": "$T$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f88101f6c5c69ddf609f728d3456a5cd29050c3649cc1f73ccad801d78727885", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ddaf7a65f5b4146db77956bad9bb507fa8ce22aea5c92e54f86f5d5b441b0ea", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe question we pose here is what should be the fibre product\n<MATH_0001>\nThe answer: A morphism from a scheme <MATH_0002> into <MATH_0003> should be a triple\n<MATH_0004> where\n<MATH_0005>, <MATH_0006> are morphisms of schemes\nand where <MATH_0007> is\nan isomorphism of elliptic curves over <MATH_0008>. This makes sense\nbecause of our definition of composition and commutative diagrams\nearlier in the discussion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e5d634074a1548d16a2423c9feed820cbdc8b1a43140a04018570ac19b0d51c", "unit_id": "tag:072L:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "inline-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "stacks-introduction.tex", "kind": "lemma", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 6780, "start": 6764}, "command_hash": "sha256:ed3a2605aa3ec7c72d20a2c1cdff2241f2b7a15c55742023bbd0b51966c661aa", "container_byte_span": {"end": 6860, "start": 6645}, "container_hash": "sha256:9d5026cd1160b362ba6bca0c9303887dcbb4d1c0ce3af8c7fb1c2e5ff7a6941a"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-key-fact", "owner_tag": "072M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:878540b6cdbdc48efab8e6db8351e1c8fba4c3c4af0e4effe84233a954bb5508", "source_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-key-fact", "usage": "root-phrase", "usage_source": {"after": "\\}", "before": ")", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "stacks-introduction-as-above", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 43, "start": 34}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": " as above"}], "source": "$T \\mapsto \\{(a, a', \\alpha)\\text{ as above}\\}$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 138, "start": 91}, "source_hash": "sha256:2d339e79476d4b14f448b69e8d9aad6d191d4c6ff9ec93ec18958665171d86c9"}], "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$T \\mapsto \\{(a, a', \\alpha)\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\}$", "MATH_0001": "$\\Sch^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$S \\times_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}} S'$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{lemma-key-fact}\n"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}[", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de40046134245a8a90a2eb4489745b16245e20c5db00aa6f2fbc32814d2c4e46", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:fc8edf8865d8b741ecb87abd767407a70c89de5760d44818349cf3331f9133ec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:14dd21b513919b1985aa38ab15242a45770743d6069bb1f5feeaa6bbabc435cf", "source_text": "Key fact<OWNARGEND_0001>The functor <MATH_0001>,\n<MATHSEG_0001> as above<MATHSEG_0002>\nis representable by a scheme <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c29729199074e280ae94d2c1fdef96b2e5737293a34935e792b8bdaa11dfaf1", "unit_id": "tag:072M:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\mathit{Isom}_{S \\times S'}(E \\times S', S \\times E')\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:441f9ee5c8ae2391c3d92c4018d3858f60dbb4c4e251ba5f416c143570392a14", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca9db878ca6b86d9181a86ebfdf6bc7a70d5a62e708d5b6c47c024dd8ba00193", "source_text": "Idea of proof. Relate this functor to\n<MATH_0001>\nand use Grothendieck's theory of Hilbert schemes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:21f04277e02a21cb47ba4d15e9481757da0088f8bf0c5d8e1da10b03026acae5", "unit_id": "tag:072M:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\times_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}} S' =\n(S \\times S')\n\\times_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1} \\times \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}}\n\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f47f9d2db766b5f8d6d0e3e6857c412653ee396bda0f4fe30cd2ceecb656cecb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8bbe9ac33526935f7abdbfaa6f8cbbcb1fa617ef092c594f7eed28b89054ebff", "source_text": "We have the formula\n<MATH_0001>.\nHence the key fact is a property of the diagonal\n<MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93c45be057eb734b0410a26cad31cdee19bdd15c7ce88060248c42ba14ca37d4", "unit_id": "tag:072N:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fabdc60fad275032e16d58e1fce47c73e52d606b5252357c2ddc78b1b416448", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn any case the key fact allows us to make the following definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0af1786259361f92f5ec2179a184d44ea8746934f638c0183505d40e81b4235e", "unit_id": "tag:072L:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\to \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "MATH_0002": "$S' \\to \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nS \\times_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}} S' \\longrightarrow S'\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dc9f0d2ab1a3a394797c259a6fdf3c0a2722d1d634c0c15a15acc44723083c3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e8a12c88d32b0e725f297018095cabc1b700175dcd0a7606696f55d8ce6779e5", "source_text": "We say a morphism <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every\nmorphism <MATH_0002> the projection morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nis smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93949fafd5955c37b2926c55b459425698c5d33f934ebe2c55c31ccff65ca343", "unit_id": "tag:072P:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6ca568f5d06e7eac8fea0bc7b3cbdf11a2a4d7863796ef3883e9c3d10bcf5350", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:edaca8ddb9f0d7dc9b8c9c54c048429d56d5c1cb9b425f8230c045a00445a813", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that this is compatible with the notion of a smooth morphism\nof schemes as the base change of a smooth morphism is smooth.\nMoreover, it is clear how to extend this definition to other properties\nof morphisms into <MATH_0001> (or your own favorite moduli stack).\nIn particular we will use it below for <TEXTITOPEN_0001>surjective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> morphisms.\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8668a96949892dff39456b59d4064cb4fd4c268aeb2e8b4f428cfb27ef2e48ea", "unit_id": "tag:072L:prose-0003"}
